      "summaries": {
        "en": "Pi-hole is a network-wide ad blocker that runs on a Raspberry Pi or other Linux device, solving the problem of intrusive ads across all connected devices without requiring individual browser extensions. It works by acting as a DNS sinkhole, intercepting and blocking ad-serving domain requests at the network level before they reach your devices. You can set it up as your network's DNS server, monitor blocked queries through its web dashboard, and customize blocklists to filter specific content types like trackers or malware domains.",
        "zh": "Pi-hole是一款部署于树莓派等Linux设备的网络级广告拦截工具，通过DNS层面拦截广告域名请求，为所有联网设备提供无侵入的广告过滤服务。其核心机制是作为DNS黑洞服务器，直接阻止广告请求到达终端，避免了传统插件需逐设备配置的繁琐。用户可将其设为家庭网络的DNS服务器，通过Web仪表板实时监控拦截状态，并支持自定义规则以屏蔽跟踪器或恶意域名，适合网络爱好者及注重隐私的用户实践使用。",
        "es": "Pi-hole is a network-wide ad blocker that runs on a Raspberry Pi or other Linux device, solving the problem of intrusive ads across all connected devices without requiring individual browser extensions. It works by acting as a DNS sinkhole, intercepting and blocking ad-serving domain requests at the network level before they reach your devices. You can set it up as your network's DNS server, monitor blocked queries through its web dashboard, and customize blocklists to filter specific content types like trackers or malware domains.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "pi-hole stands out for ad-blocker, blocker, and cloud in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Pi-hole is a network-wide ad blocker that runs on a Raspberry Pi or other Linux device, solving the problem of intrusive ads across all connected devices without requiring individual browser extensions. It works by acting as a DNS sinkhole, intercepting and blocking ad-serving domain requests at the network level before they reach your devices. You can set it up as your network's DNS server, monitor blocked queries through its web dashboard, and customize blocklists to filter specific content types like trackers or malware domains.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/pi-hole/pi-hole for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
