      "summaries": {
        "en": "WorldMonitor is an open-source global intelligence dashboard that aggregates real-time geopolitical data to provide comprehensive situational awareness. It uses AI-powered news aggregation and infrastructure tracking to filter and visualize critical information from diverse sources. Developers can deploy it locally to monitor specific regions or events, extend its TypeScript-based architecture with custom data sources, and experiment with its unified interface for OSINT research or crisis response scenarios.",
        "zh": "WorldMonitor 是一个开源实时全球情报仪表板，通过AI驱动的新闻聚合和基础设施追踪技术，整合地缘政治监控数据，提供统一态势感知界面。其核心在于利用智能算法过滤多源信息，将新闻、地理数据和监控指标可视化呈现，帮助用户快速识别关键动态。开发者可基于TypeScript架构部署本地实例，自定义数据源扩展功能，适用于区域监测、开源情报分析或应急响应等实践场景，让复杂信息变得直观可操作。",
        "es": "WorldMonitor is an open-source global intelligence dashboard that aggregates real-time geopolitical data to provide comprehensive situational awareness. It uses AI-powered news aggregation and infrastructure tracking to filter and visualize critical information from diverse sources. Developers can deploy it locally to monitor specific regions or events, extend its TypeScript-based architecture with custom data sources, and experiment with its unified interface for OSINT research or crisis response scenarios.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "worldmonitor stands out for ai, dashboard, and geopolitics in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "WorldMonitor is an open-source global intelligence dashboard that aggregates real-time geopolitical data to provide comprehensive situational awareness. It uses AI-powered news aggregation and infrastructure tracking to filter and visualize critical information from diverse sources. Developers can deploy it locally to monitor specific regions or events, extend its TypeScript-based architecture with custom data sources, and experiment with its unified interface for OSINT research or crisis response scenarios.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/koala73/worldmonitor for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
