      "summaries": {
        "en": "Xray-core is an open-source network proxy platform designed to bypass internet censorship and enhance privacy through encrypted tunneling. Its technical strength lies in supporting multiple protocols like Shadowsocks, Trojan, and TLS, allowing flexible configuration for different network environments. Developers can use it to build custom proxy solutions, experiment with traffic obfuscation techniques, or integrate it into applications requiring secure data transmission across restricted networks.",
        "zh": "Xray-core 是一个开源网络代理平台，旨在通过加密隧道技术绕过网络审查并增强隐私保护。其核心能力在于支持多种协议（如 Shadowsocks、Trojan、TLS），可灵活配置以适应不同网络环境，技术亮点包括流量混淆和协议伪装。典型使用场景包括构建自定义代理工具、研究网络穿透方法，或集成到需要安全传输数据的应用中，适合开发者实验网络自由化方案。",
        "es": "Xray-core is an open-source network proxy platform designed to bypass internet censorship and enhance privacy through encrypted tunneling. Its technical strength lies in supporting multiple protocols like Shadowsocks, Trojan, and TLS, allowing flexible configuration for different network environments. Developers can use it to build custom proxy solutions, experiment with traffic obfuscation techniques, or integrate it into applications requiring secure data transmission across restricted networks.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Xray-core stands out for anticensorship, dns, and network in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Xray-core is an open-source network proxy platform designed to bypass internet censorship and enhance privacy through encrypted tunneling. Its technical strength lies in supporting multiple protocols like Shadowsocks, Trojan, and TLS, allowing flexible configuration for different network environments. Developers can use it to build custom proxy solutions, experiment with traffic obfuscation techniques, or integrate it into applications requiring secure data transmission across restricted networks.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
